# Buried in the Garden: "Enchant land". Turn 3: Bot1 casts it ({2}{G}{W}: Forest, Mox Pearl, Mox Emerald, Island) on its own
# Forest; a creature is no legal thing to enchant. "When this Aura enters, exile target nonland permanent you don't control":
# Bot2's Grizzly Bears is the only legal target (Bot1's own Mox Pearl and Bot2's Forest, a land, are not). "Whenever
# enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional one mana of any color": a triggered mana ability that
# resolves at once (CR 605.1b, 605.4a), the color chosen as it resolves. Turn 5: Bot1 taps the Forest and chooses white, so
# the Forest's {G} and the white pay for Disenchant ({1}{W}), cast on the Aura. The Aura leaves, the Bears come back (CR
# 610.3a) under Bot2's control; the Island, not enchanted, taps for {U} alone.

